WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.162
- [Christian] Ready to open this up?

00:00:03.162 --> 00:00:04.090
- Yeah.

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:05.495
You ready?
- [Christian] Yeah.

00:00:05.495 --> 00:00:07.022
- Alright, so we open up this envelope

00:00:07.022 --> 00:00:09.286
right there in the airport and.

00:00:09.286 --> 00:00:10.869
Where are we going?

00:00:12.331 --> 00:00:15.907
(upbeat plucky music)

00:00:15.907 --> 00:00:18.194
- I hate planning vacations.

00:00:18.194 --> 00:00:20.066
- I do enjoy planning vacations.

00:00:20.066 --> 00:00:21.643
- I don't like having to find a hotel.

00:00:21.643 --> 00:00:23.850
I don't like having to find flights.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.313
I find it to be stressful.

00:00:25.313 --> 00:00:27.328
- I just, I like knowing where I'm going.

00:00:27.328 --> 00:00:28.878
I like knowing how I'm getting there.

00:00:28.878 --> 00:00:31.435
I like to time things.
I like to be punctual.

00:00:31.435 --> 00:00:34.908
- So I started to think, what
if Rob and I took a vacation

00:00:34.908 --> 00:00:36.883
where we had no control over anything.

00:00:36.883 --> 00:00:38.177
Not even the destination.

00:00:38.177 --> 00:00:41.090
I decided we would take a
trip where we would, one,

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:43.088
have no idea where we're going.

00:00:43.088 --> 00:00:45.355
Two, have to go to any restaurant

00:00:45.355 --> 00:00:47.923
or attraction that was suggested to us.

00:00:47.923 --> 00:00:52.042
And three, only order items
that were recommended.

00:00:52.042 --> 00:00:53.803
So for the first item on that checklist,

00:00:53.803 --> 00:00:55.957
I decided to book our trip using a company

00:00:55.957 --> 00:01:00.252
that specializes in mystery
vacations called Pack Up and Go.

00:01:00.252 --> 00:01:02.372
I went and filled out a questionnaire

00:01:02.372 --> 00:01:04.572
just listing all of our interests

00:01:04.572 --> 00:01:07.828
so they could match us to
the perfect destination.

00:01:07.828 --> 00:01:09.947
Craft beer and breweries, always.

00:01:09.947 --> 00:01:11.764
Vineyards and wine bars, yes.

00:01:11.764 --> 00:01:13.600
Cocktail bars, yes.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.942
So about seven days before
we're scheduled to depart,

00:01:16.942 --> 00:01:21.032
we receive an email giving
us just a few details

00:01:21.032 --> 00:01:22.503
about where we're going.

00:01:22.503 --> 00:01:26.175
- It's gonna be mid 70s and
sunny which could be anywhere.

00:01:26.175 --> 00:01:29.759
Where could we be going? I have no idea.

00:01:29.759 --> 00:01:33.303
- So about two days before our departure,

00:01:33.303 --> 00:01:37.712
I receive, in priority
mail, a big envelope.

00:01:37.712 --> 00:01:39.610
And I was, at this point I started

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:42.777
getting really excited about our trip.

00:01:46.203 --> 00:01:47.120
It feels...

00:01:48.698 --> 00:01:49.698
like Denver.

00:01:51.364 --> 00:01:52.812
Uber's outside.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.653
- Where am I hoping? It's open.

00:01:54.653 --> 00:01:56.598
- [Christian] It'd be
great if it was a city

00:01:56.598 --> 00:01:57.867
that we've never been to before.

00:01:57.867 --> 00:01:58.700
- [Rob] Yeah.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:01.028
- I have a feeling it's
Denver for some reason.

00:02:01.028 --> 00:02:04.878
- Maybe it could be Idaho.
Sun Valley's pretty cool.

00:02:04.878 --> 00:02:06.446
And I think the weather might be right.

00:02:06.446 --> 00:02:10.446
- [Uber Driver] Thank you.
- Thank you very much.

00:02:12.678 --> 00:02:14.445
Where we going, Rob?

00:02:14.445 --> 00:02:16.381
Ready to open this up?

00:02:16.381 --> 00:02:17.471
- Yeah.

00:02:17.471 --> 00:02:18.786
You ready?

00:02:18.786 --> 00:02:20.354
- Alright, so we open up this envelope

00:02:20.354 --> 00:02:22.500
right there in the airport and.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.750
Where are we going? Denver!

00:02:25.921 --> 00:02:27.691
Denver, Colorado.

00:02:27.691 --> 00:02:30.082
And I was pretty happy.

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:32.074
- We were going to Denver. I was right.

00:02:32.074 --> 00:02:33.890
- Oh here we go. Christian and Rob,

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:35.377
We are so excited to have planned

00:02:35.377 --> 00:02:37.281
this weekend getaway for you.

00:02:37.281 --> 00:02:38.994
Thanks for trusting us.

00:02:38.994 --> 00:02:40.944
We think that based on your interest in

00:02:40.944 --> 00:02:43.746
good food and drinks,
museums and the outdoors,

00:02:43.746 --> 00:02:46.506
you guys are going to
have a blast in Denver.

00:02:46.506 --> 00:02:49.839
Have a fantastic trip and happy travels.

00:02:52.649 --> 00:02:55.758
- I don't think so it's 73
degrees on Saturday and Sunday.

00:02:55.758 --> 00:02:56.925
- Yeah, but there's mountains.

00:02:56.925 --> 00:03:01.174
- I don't think we're gonna be
very close to the mountains.

00:03:01.174 --> 00:03:03.674
(funky music)

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:09.742
- We're on the plane.

00:03:09.742 --> 00:03:12.053
We know we're going to Denver, Colorado.

00:03:12.053 --> 00:03:14.189
Pulled down my little tray table,

00:03:14.189 --> 00:03:15.853
and I started making an itinerary

00:03:15.853 --> 00:03:17.374
of the places that I thought maybe,

00:03:17.374 --> 00:03:19.128
out of what Pack Up and Go gave us,

00:03:19.128 --> 00:03:20.499
we would want to hit up.

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:24.214
- We promised ourselves we would
hit up as many as we could.

00:03:24.214 --> 00:03:27.230
Unless we met somebody who recommended

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.661
we check out someplace else.

00:03:28.661 --> 00:03:30.871
- Denver, here we are.

00:03:30.871 --> 00:03:33.371
(funky music)

00:03:41.425 --> 00:03:44.149
- So one of the first
people we met in Denver

00:03:44.149 --> 00:03:48.097
reminded us that recreational
marijuana is legal in Colorado

00:03:48.097 --> 00:03:51.238
and he recommended that
we check out a dispensary.

00:03:51.238 --> 00:03:53.054
- We're walking past and it's, like,

00:03:53.054 --> 00:03:54.861
they're as common as a 7-Eleven

00:03:54.861 --> 00:03:56.327
or a Starbucks here in New York.

00:03:56.327 --> 00:03:57.862
Unfortunately there's no footage though

00:03:57.862 --> 00:03:59.702
because they don't allow cameras inside.

00:03:59.702 --> 00:04:01.293
It's a very private experience.

00:04:01.293 --> 00:04:03.505
- Okay, so we are now on our way

00:04:03.505 --> 00:04:07.125
to a restaurant called Guard and Grace.

00:04:07.125 --> 00:04:08.014
- That's correct.

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:10.434
- Guard and Grace was a
recommendation from Pack Up and Go.

00:04:10.434 --> 00:04:14.701
They actually booked a reservation for us.

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:18.701
- I cannot speak highly
enough about this place.

00:04:20.203 --> 00:04:21.914
- [Christian] As per the rules,

00:04:21.914 --> 00:04:25.170
we had to ask the waiter
for his suggestions.

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:28.618
- And every single dish that
he recommended and we ate.

00:04:28.618 --> 00:04:31.306
It just smashed it.
Knocked it out of the park.

00:04:31.306 --> 00:04:32.873
- [Christian] It was one of the best meals

00:04:32.873 --> 00:04:35.524
I've ever had at a restaurant.

00:04:35.524 --> 00:04:37.273
And I really think it was important

00:04:37.273 --> 00:04:40.640
just listening to this
guy that knows the menu.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:42.674
The next morning we ate at
a popular breakfast spot

00:04:42.674 --> 00:04:44.455
that we had heard about.

00:04:44.455 --> 00:04:47.081
And there a waitress
recommended we check out

00:04:47.081 --> 00:04:49.264
a few of the breweries
that are in that area.

00:04:49.264 --> 00:04:50.951
We borrowed bikes from our hotel

00:04:50.951 --> 00:04:54.000
and literally hit up
every one she mentioned.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.550
- Alright, so we are on our way now

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:59.467
to the first of our
brewing company bike crawl.

00:05:01.199 --> 00:05:03.032
These are all Wynkoop.

00:05:04.215 --> 00:05:06.120
Alright, what do you recommend?

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:08.942
If a bartender recommended
a beer, we drank it.

00:05:08.942 --> 00:05:11.520
And if someone suggested
a different brewery,

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:12.687
then we went there.

00:05:12.687 --> 00:05:16.054
West coast IPA, hoppy,
orange pith and bitter.

00:05:16.054 --> 00:05:18.751
It's an Indian pale ale.

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:22.120
(lips smacking)

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.575
- Not so much.

00:05:23.575 --> 00:05:26.158
(upbeat music)

00:05:39.192 --> 00:05:41.109
- Sprechen sie Deutsch?

00:05:42.092 --> 00:05:45.334
- The best part about Denver, hands down,

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:48.417
was a suggestion from Pack Up and Go.

00:05:49.377 --> 00:05:54.221
They recommended we go to Red
Rocks at 5:30 in the morning.

00:05:54.221 --> 00:05:55.916
- [Rob] We had to jump in an Uber,

00:05:55.916 --> 00:05:58.662
travel 45 minutes into the
start of the Rocky Mountains

00:05:58.662 --> 00:06:01.454
and we're going to the
Red Rock National Park

00:06:01.454 --> 00:06:03.254
to watch the sun rise.

00:06:03.254 --> 00:06:05.460
- [Christian] The video
doesn't really do justice

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:06.806
to what it looked like.

00:06:06.806 --> 00:06:09.436
Just seeing those colors mixed with

00:06:09.436 --> 00:06:11.740
the red rocks that were surrounding us.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:15.798
- [Rob] It was the most beautiful
moment of the entire trip.

00:06:15.798 --> 00:06:17.221
Everything you could ever ask for

00:06:17.221 --> 00:06:18.260
sitting there waiting for that sun

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:21.104
to come up overlooking Denver.

00:06:21.104 --> 00:06:24.353
- And after sunrise, we met
somebody who recommended

00:06:24.353 --> 00:06:26.194
that we do one of the longer hiking trails

00:06:26.194 --> 00:06:29.184
that's in that area and we did it.

00:06:29.184 --> 00:06:33.368
Although, we weren't quite
dressed appropriately for it.

00:06:33.368 --> 00:06:35.417
- To be honest, like, something
I've learned about myself

00:06:35.417 --> 00:06:36.551
on this trip, like,

00:06:36.551 --> 00:06:40.888
it is really nice to
embrace ambiguity sometimes.

00:06:40.888 --> 00:06:42.472
Just kinda go with the flow.

00:06:42.472 --> 00:06:46.687
Damn, like, that a really
fantastic way to live life.

00:06:46.687 --> 00:06:49.372
If I could just sort of
blow that out a little bit

00:06:49.372 --> 00:06:51.998
and practice that in general overall.

00:06:51.998 --> 00:06:54.400
- I wish I could only
go on mystery vacations.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:56.912
- [Rob] Yeah, there is so much power

00:06:56.912 --> 00:07:00.823
in letting someone else
plan things for you.

00:07:00.823 --> 00:07:03.323
(calm music)

